.TH MILLENNIUM\-CONFIG 1 "August 7, 2026" "millennium-helpers" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
millennium-config \- manage Millennium client settings without the Steam UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B millennium config
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads and updates the Millennium client's own configuration while preserving
unknown settings. Mutations use an atomic file replacement. Restart Steam
after changing plugin or theme activation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B show
Show the active theme, update settings, and enabled plugins.
.TP
.B plugins
List installed plugins and whether each one is enabled.
.TP
.B themes
List installed themes and mark the active theme.
.TP
.B errors
Scan the current session in detected Steam web logs and report errors that
contain a direct installed plugin or theme source path. Recognized startup
markers exclude retained entries from earlier sessions.
.TP
.BI enable " NAME..."
Enable one or more installed plugins.
.TP
.BI disable " NAME..."
Disable one or more plugins.
.TP
.BI theme " NAME"
Select an installed theme.
.TP
.BI disable-theme " [NAME]"
Reset the active theme to Steam. When NAME is supplied, refuse the change if a
different theme is active.
.TP
.B disable-errors
Disable enabled plugins with directly attributed errors and reset an affected
active theme to Steam. Requires
.B --yes
unless
.B --dry-run
is used.
Use
.B --plugins-only
or
.B --themes-only
to limit remediation to one component kind.
.SH OPTIONS
.\" @@cli-contract:commands.config.man_options@@
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output show, plugins, themes, or errors results as structured JSON.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show configuration changes without writing them.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress informational output after configuration changes.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Confirm disabling every enabled component with directly attributed errors.
.TP
.B \-\-plugins\-only
With disable-errors, disable only enabled plugins with directly attributed errors.
.TP
.B \-\-themes\-only
With disable-errors, disable only the active theme when it has directly attributed errors.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message.
.\" @@/cli-contract:commands.config.man_options@@
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B millennium config show
.TP
.B millennium config plugins
.TP
.B millennium config disable gratitude extendium
.TP
.B millennium config theme Steam
.TP
.B millennium config errors
.TP
.B millennium config disable-errors --dry-run
.TP
.B millennium config disable-errors --plugins-only --yes
.TP
.B millennium config disable-errors --themes-only --yes
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/millennium/config.json
is the usual Linux client configuration. Platform and Flatpak locations are
detected automatically.
